  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The book is intentionally designed not to be openable from either side.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">In slipcase.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Includes 1 folded sheet (28 cm.) containing statement about the book by the author.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The book contains a cycle of 27 poems by myself, Simic and Ristovic, all of them concerning the Devil or humans behaving in devilish ways.... The structure is a variation on an ordinary casebound book.... The variation is that half of the signatures are sewn together on the right-hand side, and half on the left, alternating through the text block (it is really like two separately sewn text blocks slid together). "--Author's statement.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Largely inspired by an untitled poem by Aleksandar Ristovic as translated by Charles Simic, which contains the line: "Time of fools is coming, time of the know-nothing professor and the book that cannot be cracked open at either edge."--Cf. author's statement.</subfield>
  </datafield>
